WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.750
Now the orphan rule itself.

2
00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:05.996
The plan's decision, owned by the
chief information security officer,

3
00:00:05.996 --> 00:00:10.168
is to disable first, once the
identity governance officer confirms,

4
00:00:10.168 --> 00:00:12.850
then give the office
thirty days to claim it.

5
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.720
Access and Privilege's own
policy runs the other way round,

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.107
thirty days to assign an
owner and then suspension,

7
00:00:20.107 --> 00:00:24.300
but the program's rule is settled:
the plan's order, disable first.

8
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.650
Learn agrees on the shape:
disable, don't delete.

9
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.175
It offers two reversible switches.

10
00:00:30.175 --> 00:00:33.112
One deactivates the
registration everywhere,

11
00:00:33.112 --> 00:00:36.050
but its procedure is still
on the beta endpoint.

12
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.957
The other disables sign-in in this
tenant on the stable endpoint,

13
00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:41.860
and that's the one the code uses.
